# angle_doubling: rational angles on `Q/Z` under `t -> 2t`.
#
#   angle   Angle, an exactly reduced `p/q` modulo one, with the doubling
#           map, the orbit, and the exact preperiod and period of every
#           rational angle in closed form.
#
# Specification: docs/rational-interval-arithmetic-spec.md, section 1.
#
# This is finite combinatorics on `Q/Z`, not geometry. No angle here is
# derived from a locus, no locus is derived from an angle, and nothing in the
# package knows what a ray is. What a consumer does with the correspondence
# between an angle's type and a dynamical point's type is the consumer's
# import to name and gate.
